        \end{array} \right\rbrack$ into $\left\lbrack \begin{array}{r}
        {- 1} \\
        3
        \end{array} \right\rbrack$. Use the fact that $T$ is linear to find the images under $T$ of $3\mathbf{u}$, $2\mathbf{v}$, and $3\mathbf{u} + 2\mathbf{v}$.

Let $\mathbf{e}_{1} = \,\,\left\lbrack \begin{array}{r}
        1 \\
        0
        \end{array} \right\rbrack$, $\mathbf{e}_{2} = \,\,\left\lbrack \begin{array}{r}
        0 \\
        1
        \end{array} \right\rbrack$, $\mathbf{y}_{1} = \,\,\left\lbrack \begin{array}{r}
        2 \\
        5
        \end{array} \right\rbrack$, and $\mathbf{y}_{2} = \,\,\left\lbrack \begin{array}{r}
        {- 1} \\
        6
        \end{array} \right\rbrack$, and let $T:\text{ℝ}^{2}\rightarrow\text{ℝ}^{2}$ be a linear transformation that maps $\mathbf{e}_{1}$ into $\mathbf{y}_{1}$ and maps $\mathbf{e}_{2}$ into $\mathbf{y}_{2}$. Find the images of $\left\lbrack \begin{array}{r}
        5 \\
        {- 3}
        \end{array} \right\rbrack$ and $\left\lbrack \begin{array}{r}
        x_{1} \\
        x_{2}
        \end{array} \right\rbrack$.

Let $\mathbf{x} = \,\,\left\lbrack \begin{array}{r}
        x_{1} \\
        x_{2}
        \end{array} \right\rbrack$, $\mathbf{v}_{1} = \,\,\left\lbrack \begin{array}{r}
        {- 2} \\
        5
        \end{array} \right\rbrack$, and $\mathbf{v}_{2} = \,\,\left\lbrack \begin{array}{r}
        7 \\
        {- 3}
        \end{array} \right\rbrack$, and let $T:\text{ℝ}^{2}\rightarrow\text{ℝ}^{2}$ be a linear transformation that maps $\mathbf{x}$ into $x_{1}\mathbf{v}_{1} + x_{2}\mathbf{v}_{2}$. Find a matrix $A$ such that $T(\mathbf{x})$ is $A\mathbf{x}$ for each $\mathbf{x}$.

[T] Let $\mathbf{b} = \left\lbrack \begin{array}{r}
        {- 7} \\
        {- 7} \\
        13 \\
        {- 5}
        \end{array} \right\rbrack$ and let $A$ be the matrix in Exercise 46. Is $\mathbf{b}$ in the range of the transformation $\mathbf{x}\mapsto A{\mathbf{x}\text{?}}$ If so, find an $\mathbf{x}$ whose image under the transformation is $\mathbf{b}$.

example.paragraph:
The columns of $I_{2} = \,\begin{bmatrix}
