        0
        \end{bmatrix}$ and $\mathbf{e}_{2} = \,\begin{bmatrix}
        0 \\
        1
        \end{bmatrix}$. Suppose $T$ is a linear transformation from $\text{ℝ}^{2}$ into $\text{ℝ}^{3}$ such that

paragraph.math:
$$\begin{matrix}
        {T(\mathbf{x})} & {= T(x_{1}\mathbf{e}_{1} + \cdots + x_{n}\mathbf{e}_{n}) = x_{1}T(\mathbf{e}_{1}) + \cdots + x_{n}T(\mathbf{e}_{n})} \\
         & {= \left\lbrack \begin{array}{rlr}
