statement.paragraph:
[T] College Moving Truck Rental has a fleet of $20$, $100$, and $200$ trucks in Pullman, Spokane, and Seattle, respectively. A truck rented at one location may be returned to any of the three locations. The various fractions of trucks returned to the three locations each month are shown in the matrix below. What will be the approximate distribution of the trucks after three months?$$\begin{array}{l}
        {\mspace{27mu}\text{Trucks}\,\text{Rented}\,\text{From:}} \\
        {\text{Pullman}\mspace{9mu}\text{Spokane}\mspace{9mu}\text{Seattle}\mspace{23mu}\text{   }\mspace{-4mu}\mspace{-4mu}\text{Returned To:}} \\
        {{\;\left\lbrack \begin{array}{lll}
        .30 & {\mspace{40mu}.15} & {\mspace{40mu}.05} \\
        .30 & {\mspace{40mu}.70} & {\mspace{40mu}.05} \\
        .40 & {\mspace{40mu}.15} & {\mspace{40mu}.90}
        \end{array} \right\rbrack}\begin{array}{l}
        {\mspace{27mu}\text{Airport}} \\
        {\mspace{27mu}\text{East}} \\
        {\mspace{27mu}\text{West}}
        \end{array}}
        \end{array}$$

[T] Budget® Rent a Car in Wichita, Kansas, has a fleet of about $500$ cars, at three locations. A car rented at one location may be returned to any of the three locations. The various fractions of cars returned to the three locations are shown in the matrix below. Suppose that on Monday there are $295$ cars at the airport (or rented from there), $55$ cars at the east side office, and $150$ cars at the west side office. What will be the approximate distribution of cars on Wednesday?$$\begin{array}{l}
        {\mspace{32mu}\text{Cars}\,\text{Rented}\,\text{From:}} \\
        {\text{Airport}\mspace{27mu}\text{East}\qquad\text{West}\mspace{27mu}\mspace{6mu}\mspace{-4mu}\text{  }\mspace{-4mu}\text{Returned To:}} \\
        {\left\lbrack \begin{array}{lll}
        .97 & {\mspace{40mu}.05} & {\mspace{40mu}.10} \\
        .00 & {\mspace{40mu}.90} & {\mspace{40mu}.05} \\
        .03 & {\mspace{40mu}.05} & {\mspace{40mu}.85}
        \end{array} \right\rbrack\begin{array}{l}
        {\mspace{27mu}\text{Airport}} \\
        {\mspace{27mu}\text{East}} \\
        {\mspace{27mu}\text{West}}
        \end{array}}
        \end{array}$$

Determine the value(s) of $a$ such that $\left\{ {\left\lbrack \begin{array}{r}
      1 \\
      a
      \end{array} \right\rbrack\text{,~}\begin{bmatrix}
      a \\
      {a + 2}
      \end{bmatrix}} \right\}$ is linearly independent.
